# Commit the one deployment record that is true; keep the 37 pre-reset / aspirational files out
# of the index (they reference 173 addresses that have no code on chain 724). The negation only
# works because this rule excludes the *contents* — `deployments/` alone would make
# `!deployments/lxon-chain-724.json` a no-op, since git cannot re-include a file under an
# excluded directory.
apps/contracts/deployments/*
!apps/contracts/deployments/lxon-chain-724.json
# The trust index for this directory. It has to be re-included explicitly: the 37 ignored records
# around it are exactly why a written-down conclusion about them is worth versioning, and an ignored
# README reaches nobody — not a clone, not a review, not CI.
!apps/contracts/deployments/README.md
RELEASE_MANIFEST.json
# lxon-evm-node was ignored wholesale because of the QBFT validator key inside it. Ignore the
# keys and the data dirs by name instead, so the genesis file, the RPC-hardening entrypoint, the
# compose stacks and every ops script are versioned. 26 of the 30 files outside the data dirs are
# source; 4 are secrets. Verified in a scratch repo before this change.
lxon-evm-node/**/privatekey*.txt
lxon-evm-node/**/nodekey
lxon-evm-node/**/password*.txt
lxon-evm-node/**/*.pem
lxon-evm-node/**/*.jks
lxon-evm-node/**/keystore*/
lxon-evm-node/geth/data/
lxon-evm-node/besu/data/
# Bridge signing validators (added 2026-10-21 so minConfirmations=2 has real signers). These
# are throwaway signing accounts, not the QBFT validator key, but they are still key material
# and are used by `cast send` from scripts — the whole directory stays untracked. Rule shape
# matters: `validators/` would block re-including anything later, so exclude the contents.
lxon-evm-node/besu/validators/*

# Local 725/726 QBFT testbed: throwaway validator keys and blockstores. The generated
# genesis.json files ARE versioned (public data); nothing under keys/ or */node-*/ is.
# `besu operator generate-blockchain-config --to=<dir>` writes a directory per node there
# (key + key.pub), so */raw/ is ignored even though make-genesis.py now builds outside the repo.
lxon-evm-node/besu/testnet/keys/*
lxon-evm-node/besu/testnet/725/node-*/
lxon-evm-node/besu/testnet/726/node-*/
lxon-evm-node/besu/testnet/*/raw/
lxon-evm-node/besu/testnet/__pycache__/
# Python bytecode dirs are never a deliverable, and running a checker with py_compile drops one
# wherever the imported module lives (script/polygon137/lib/ gained one on 2026-10-28). Nothing in
# this repository tracks a __pycache__ file, so the broad rule cannot shadow a real one.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# N2: `besu operator generate-blockchain-config` writes real node private keys into a temporary
# directory (gen/keys/<addr>/key). make-genesis.py builds it outside the repo and sweeps survivors,
# but a SIGKILL honours neither, and the paths above do not match that shape -- so these two rules
# are the last line of defence against a survivor being staged by an indiscriminate `git add -A`.
besu-operator-*
**/gen/keys/

lxon-evm-node/**/.env
lxon-evm-node/**/.env.*
!lxon-evm-node/.env.example
deployment/chainlist/ethereum-lists/_data/icons/lxon.json

# Rust build artifacts
/target/
**/target/

# Vendored Foundry libraries. lib/forge-std is an embedded git repo that .gitmodules never
# declared, so it can only land as a gitlink or a snapshot; restore with `forge install`.
apps/contracts/lib/
lxon-evm-node/besu/testnet/enode-1.txt
